A||||2||b_b_a_d||Fuel leak / Bad gas mileage||||3||
Z||000000||b_b_a_d||03-10-2000||02:41 AM||||Well here goes.<P>I discovered a nice hole in the fuel line from the filter to the injectors.<P>The cause:  Minor engine vibration or what have you causing the hose to rub up against the sharp edge on the bottom of the battery tray!  <P>I pulled the fuel line off in about 20 minutes or so.  (no beer)<P>A note to all...  When relieving the pressure in the fuel line with the fuel pump fuse out, be sure to turn her over more than 5 times!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">   Can we say squirt squirt squirt...   Arghhhh  my eyes my eyes  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>I was expecting a little bit of pressure still so I was prepared to get saturated with gasoline.  Thank God my wife wasn't out there otherwise I would be a human fireball the way she smokes and works on cars.  <P>Anyway, to the point...<P>Has anyone else had this problem?  If so, what did you do to keep the fuel line away from the tray?  Outside of the obvious wire tie thing and batboys battery project does anybody have any ideas?<P>After I get this all hooked up again, I will check my gas mileage one more time!<BR>My wife took the car today and put less than 12 miles on a full tank of gas.  To give you an idea how bad it had become, there was only a 1/4 tank of gas left when I was working on the car.  DOH!!!     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by b_b_a_d (edited 03-10-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000001||batboy||03-10-2000||07:33 AM||||I've done this before, take a small piece of heater hose and slip it onto the fuel line at the point where it rubs for extra protection. You may have to lightly clamp it on. Most parts store sell different size hoses in bulk, so you can get a 1/2 foot of it or so for cheap. The redneck way of doing it would be to wrap some duct tape around the rub point. Might look tacky, but it works. Of course, these suggestions are meant to be done AFTER the old fuel line is replaced with a new one.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 03-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||03-10-2000||07:42 AM||||My Fieo has a ribbed plastic tubing cut lengthwise over both fuel lines. I'm pretty sure it is factory, maybe yours was pulled by a previous owner.||||reg||1
